# bouyzero_founders_gmail_node.md

## 1. Node Definition
This node represents the first operational buoy record in the United States market branch.
It stores manually parsed information derived from the Founder’s email account that relates to
accounts, vendors, and services that are in the process of transitioning to Sentinel Labs LLC.

## 2. Purpose
The node provides a centralized record of:
- existing vendor relationships prior to formal incorporation
- accounts currently registered under the Founder’s personal name
- accounts that will be migrated to Sentinel Labs LLC as entity onboarding completes
- email-based interactions relevant to trade accounts, billing, onboarding, or authentication

## 3. Scope of Data
This node may contain:
- vendor names
- account types
- service categories
- transition status indicators
- notes derived from Founder-to-vendor email exchanges

This node does **not** contain:
- raw emails
- personal content unrelated to company onboarding
- private communications outside the scope of business account migration

## 4. Transition Objective
All relationships tracked in this node are expected to become formal Sentinel Labs LLC accounts.
The node exists to ensure a complete and ordered migration process as entity creation,
vendor onboarding, and buoy deployment proceed.

## 5. Relationship Classification
Each entry should include:
- vendor/service name
- current registration state (personal / mixed / converting / complete)
- required actions (if any)
- target Sentinel Labs LLC address or buoy endpoint
- date of last related communication

